you can ask like a physician, how statistically likely is something? What is the probability of something happening? Or if you're given too many options or too much information, you can ask a professional to simplify, the information. So that to whatever is the most important information in their view. And by doing that, people actually will understand more. Sometimes less can be more. What about the people who need to convey numerical information, whether that's doctors talking to patients or maybe journalists explaining economic data, scientists who are trying to explain climate risk? How can they help people better understand the numbers they're putting out there so that we can make better decisions?
你可以问像医生那样，某件事在统计学上有多大可能？某事发生的概率是多少？或者如果你被给予太多的选择或太多的信息，你可以要求专业人士简化信息。所以，以他们看来最重要的信息为准。通过这样做，人们实际上会理解更多。有时少即是多。那么那些需要传达数字信息的人呢，无论是医生与病人交谈，还是记者解释经济数据，科学家试图解释气候风险？他们如何帮助人们更好地理解他们发布的数据，以便我们能够做出更好的决策？

